The five findings that matter, all small:

1. **About's anchors don't move the focus.** Arriving at `/about#owners` (from Home's owners card) or `/about#contact` (from the footer) scrolls to the section, but the focus stays at the top of the page. A screen reader starts reading from the page title, and the next Tab jumps back up to the top. Fixing it changes S8's focus rule, so you'd approve it first.
2. **About's note says «تواصل معنا» twice.** The note already ends with «تواصل معنا.», and the page adds a link with the same words after it. It's visible in the 1440 screenshot. The fix is to make the sentence's own last words the link.
3. **Home's owners card doesn't say the status shows automatically.** Design issue 36 asks for that, but the plan's own Arabic text for the card leaves it out. The code follows that text word for word, so this is your wording call.
4. **Home's heading can mislabel the cards.** On a slow connection, after near me is granted, the heading switches to «المساحات الأقرب إليك» while the "available now" cards are still on screen.
5. **A second retry while offline says nothing.** Pressing «إعادة المحاولة» again while still offline gives a screen reader no new announcement.

